        "question_title": "\\(y\\) varies inversely as \\(x^2\\). If \\(y=18\\) when \\(x=2\\), find the positive value of \\(x\\) when \\(y=8\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Since \\(y\\\\propto\\\\frac{1}{x^2}\\), \\(x^2y=k\\). Hence \\(k=2^2\\\\times18=72\\). For \\(y=8\\), \\(x^2=\\\\frac{72}{8}=9\\), so the positive value is \\(x=3\\).",
